# Laboratory Page — YouCam Apparel VTO Integration

Build a fully functional virtual try-on experience in the **Laboratory** page using YouCam's generative Apparel VTO API, so shoppers can see how clothes look on them before buying.

## Current State

- **`src/data/apiFetch.js`** — Contains working API logic (start task → poll) but:
  - Uses hardcoded sample URLs instead of user-uploaded images
  - Uses `src_file_url` / `ref_file_url` (public URL approach), which works when images are publicly hosted
  - Self-executes via an IIFE at import time (not usable as a callable service)
  - Not TypeScript, no error handling for the UI
- **`src/pages/lab/Laboratory.tsx`** — Empty shell (`<div>Laboratory</div>`)
- **No CORS proxy** — The YouCam API (`yce-api-01.makeupar.com`) will block direct browser requests. We need a Vite dev proxy.

## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **API Key**: Do you already have a `.env` file with `VITE_YOUCAM_API_KEY` set? I see it referenced in `apiFetch.js` but `.env` is gitignored. I'll write the code assuming it exists — please confirm you have a valid key or I can add a placeholder.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Image Sources**: The current `apiFetch.js` uses YouCam's sample hosted URLs (`src_file_url` / `ref_file_url`). The two integration approaches are:
> 1. **Public URL approach** (current) — User pastes a URL or we use pre-selected garment images. Simpler, no file upload needed.
> 2. **File Upload approach** — User uploads their own photo from disk. This requires the YouCam File Upload API (`/s2s/v2.0/file`) to get a `file_id`, then using `src_file_id` / `ref_file_id` in the task request.
> 
> **I plan to support both**: Pre-curated garments (public URLs) + user photo upload. The user photo will be uploaded via the File API, garments will use public URLs. Let me know if you have a preference.

## Proposed Changes

### Vite Dev Proxy (CORS fix)

#### [MODIFY] [vite.config.ts](file:///c:/Users/adeoy/PROG/Drip_match/vite.config.ts)
Add a proxy rule so browser requests to `/api/youcam/` are forwarded to `https://yce-api-01.makeupar.com`, bypassing CORS in development.

```ts
server: {
  proxy: {
    '/api/youcam': {
      target: 'https://yce-api-01.makeupar.com',
      changeOrigin: true,
      rewrite: (path) => path.replace(/^\/api\/youcam/, ''),
    }
  }
}
```

---

### API Service Layer

#### [NEW] [youCamService.ts](file:///c:/Users/adeoy/PROG/Drip_match/src/services/youCamService.ts)
A proper TypeScript module exporting reusable async functions:

- **`startTryOnTask(garmentUrl, referenceUrl, category?)`** — POST to start a cloth VTO task using public URLs
- **`uploadFile(file: File)`** — Upload a user photo via the File API, returns a `file_id`
- **`startTryOnTaskWithFileIds(srcFileId, refFileId, category?)`** — POST using file IDs instead of URLs
- **`pollTaskResult(taskId)`** — Poll until success/error, with configurable intervals
- **Types**: `TryOnResult`, `TaskStatus`, `GarmentCategory`

This replaces the self-executing `apiFetch.js`. The old file will remain for reference but won't be imported.

---

### Laboratory Page (main feature)

#### [NEW] [Laboratory.tsx](file:///c:/Users/adeoy/PROG/Drip_match/src/pages/lab/Laboratory.tsx) (overwrite)
A premium, multi-step virtual try-on interface:

**Layout — 3 panels:**
1. **Garment Selection Panel** (left) — Grid of pre-curated garment images with category tabs (Tops, Bottoms, Full Outfits). Clicking a garment selects it.
2. **Try-On Stage** (center) — The main area showing:
   - Upload zone for the user's reference photo (drag & drop + click to browse)
   - Once both garment + photo are selected → "Try It On" CTA button
   - Loading state with animated progress indicator during API processing
   - Result display with before/after comparison slider
3. **Details & Actions Panel** (right) — Shows garment info, confidence tips, and action buttons (Save to Favorites, Try Another)

**Visual design:**
- Dark-mode-first, consistent with your existing `--bg-color` / `--text-color` system
- Glassmorphism cards with subtle backdrop blur
- Animated transitions between steps (Framer Motion)
- Red-800 accent color matching your existing CTA buttons
- Responsive: stacks vertically on mobile

#### [NEW] [laboratory.module.css](file:///c:/Users/adeoy/PROG/Drip_match/src/pages/lab/laboratory.module.css)
Scoped styles for the Laboratory page — glassmorphism panels, drop zone animations, before/after slider, loading states.

